import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="WINSERV | Privacy"
  description="How the Winserv website handles the data of its visitors: an access log, aggregate statistics, no cookies."
  path="/en/privacy.html"
>
<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="section-label">Company</div>
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p>What this website records, why, and for how long</p>
</div>
<section class="section--text">
  <div class="article-wrap">
    <div class="article-body">
      <h2 class="article-h3">Who the controller is</h2>
      <p>M. SAMOILENKO INFORMATICA, trading as <span lang="pt-BR">WinServ Tecnologia da Informação</span>, CNPJ 10.411.266/0001-80, <span lang="pt-BR">Av. Almirante Tamandaré, 106, apto 201, Vila Nossa Senhora dos Navegantes, Rio Grande/RS, CEP 96202-570</span>, Brazil.</p>
      <p>The data protection officer is Marcelo Samoilenko, at <a class="link-blue" href="mailto:dpo@winserv.com.br">dpo@winserv.com.br</a>. He receives requests and complaints from data subjects and answers communications from the ANPD, Brazil's data protection authority.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h3">What this website records</h2>
      <p>Each visit creates a record with the IP address, the date and time, the page requested, the referring page (when your browser sends it) and the browser's identification. The website runs on a server in Germany, in the European Union (Hetzner Online GmbH).</p>

      <h2 class="article-h3">Why, and for how long</h2>
      <p>We keep these records for 6 months (185 days) and then discard them, as Brazil's Internet Civil Framework (Marco Civil da Internet, art. 15) asks of anyone who runs an internet application.</p>
      <p>We use the same records, only in aggregate, to learn which pages are read, where visits come from and how many times someone clicks an e-mail address on the site. These are counts: we build no profile, do not identify who visited and do not combine this data with anything else.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h3">Cookies</h2>
      <p>This website sets no cookies and loads no third-party tools — no analytics, no advertising, no external fonts.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h3">When you write to us</h2>
      <p>A message to <a class="link-blue" href="mailto:comercial@winserv.com.br">comercial@winserv.com.br</a> or <a class="link-blue" href="mailto:dpo@winserv.com.br">dpo@winserv.com.br</a> reaches WinServ's mailbox on Microsoft 365, stored in the United States. Writing is optional, nothing on the site depends on it, and the message is used only to reply.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h3">Links that leave the site</h2>
      <p>The site's external links — such as WhatsApp, LinkedIn and the services mentioned in the articles — only take data of yours to those services if you click them; from then on each service's own rules apply.</p>

      <h2 class="article-h3">Your rights</h2>
      <p>You may ask the data protection officer for confirmation, access, correction or deletion of your data, and the other measures in art. 18 of the LGPD, Brazil's General Data Protection Law. You may also complain to the national data protection authority (<span lang="pt-BR">Autoridade Nacional de Proteção de Dados</span>).</p>

      <h2 class="article-h3">Winserv WiFi</h2>
      <p>The Winserv WiFi product has its own notice, at <a class="link-blue" href="https://www.wifi.winserv.com.br/privacy/">www.wifi.winserv.com.br/privacy</a>.</p>

      <p class="article-note">Marcelo Samoilenko, owner of M. SAMOILENKO INFORMATICA and data protection officer. Version of October 8, 2026.</p>
      <p class="article-note">This is a translation; if it differs from the Portuguese version, the Portuguese version prevails.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
